            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Ramses II's Early Life</strong><br>\nRamses II was one of Egypt's most powerful pharaohs, born around 1303 BCE. He was appointed prince regent by his father, Pharaoh Seti I, at a young age. Ramses II was trained in archery, horsemanship, and warfare to prepare him for his future role as a ruler. His early life was about learning statecraft and military skills, which were crucial for leading Egypt.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Ascension to the Throne</strong><br>\nUpon Seti I's death, Ramses II ascended to the throne as Egypt's ruler. He began his reign over an empire that stretched from the Nile's delta in the north to Nubia in the south. His coronation was a grand affair and marked the beginning of what would be a lengthy rule. Ramses II's reign was distinguished by his ambition to construct monuments and cities.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Military Campaigns</strong><br>\nRamses II is perhaps best known for his military campaigns. He sought to recapture the territory in modern-day Syria that was contested by the Hittites. His most famous battle, the Battle of Kadesh, took place in 1274 BCE and was initially claimed as a victory by Ramses II, though historians now believe it ended in a stalemate.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
