            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Battle of Kadesh</strong><br>\nThe Battle of Kadesh is often touted as one of the largest chariot battles ever fought. Ramses II led an army of 20,000 men against the Hittites in this conflict. Despite being caught in a Hittite ambush and suffering initial setbacks, Ramses rallied his troops and fought to a draw, which he celebrated as a personal success.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Building Projects</strong><br>\nRamses II was also a great builder whose projects included the construction of vast temple complexes at Karnak and Luxor. He built the famous Abu Simbel temples, which were carved out of a mountainside and designed to intimidate Egypt's enemies and impress its friends with the might of the Egyptian empire.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Treaty with the Hittites</strong><br>\nAfter years of warfare, Ramses II negotiated a peace treaty with the Hittites. This treaty is considered one of the earliest recorded peace agreements in history. It brought stability to the region and allowed Ramses II to focus on internal developments and building projects in Egypt.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
